casebook unsatisfied-fixture v1
source "adversarial fixture for the Unsatisfied outcome (not a real asset)" dated 2026-09-22 by "quorum tests"
note "This casebook is DELIBERATELY BROKEN and cbc must refuse it. Do not fix it."
note ""
note "`Unsatisfied` means the casebook decisively rejects every action it declared. It is a casebook defect, not an"
note "ambiguous plant, and the arbiter reports it separately for exactly that reason -- conflating it with"
note "Indeterminate would send an engineer to look at the equipment when the document is what is wrong."
note ""
note "The mistake here is the one that makes it happen in practice: giving the IDLE action a condition. An idle"
note "action is what survives when nothing else fires, so it must have no conditions at all. Give it one, and any"
note "state where that condition fails and no other action applies rejects everything."
note ""
note "Neither real casebook can test this: both report Unsatisfied in 0 of their states, which is what a correct"
note "casebook does. That is precisely why a fixture is needed -- realistic data proves the realistic data does not"
note "trip the bug."

observe x "condition x asserted"
observe y "condition y asserted"

claim cx "x holds" needs x
claim cy "y holds" needs y

# The defect: the idle action is gated on cy, so when neither x nor y is asserted nothing at all can be selected.
action idle_act idle when cy
action act_on   safe when cx
prefer act_on over idle_act
